ailability"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01UskSCE6jZLysD3XeDUJCEZ","tool_input":{"command":"ls /Applications","description":"List installed applications"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FaCJpYDTbhmrHzyc71MjwX","tool_input":{"command":"cat > build/build.js <<'EOF'\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst root = path.resolve(__dirname, '..');\nconst css = fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, 'inputs/lys/lys.css'), 'utf8');\nconst js = fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, 'inputs/lys/lys.iife.js'), 'utf8');\nif (/<\\/(style|script)/i.test(css + js)) throw new Error('inline asset contains closing tag');\nconst tpl = fs.readFileSync(path.join(__dirname, 'template.html'), 'utf8');\nconst jsWithNotice = '/* Lys 1.2.1 runtime, MIT (https://github.com/villetakanen/lys), vendored unmodified; see inputs/lys/NOTICE.md */\\n' + js.trimEnd();\nconst out = tpl.replace('/*LYS_CSS*/', () => css.trimEnd()).replace('/*LYS_JS*/', () => jsWithNotice);\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, 'output/slide.html'), out);\nconst decision = {\n  protocol: 'kata-eval-decision/v1',\n  audience_question: 'Which retrofit barrier is most common overall, and did service turnaround improve?',\n  form: 'Separate-source aligned bars (each source on its own denominator) with a text-first turnaround assessment',\n  fit_rationale: 'Within Partner North, one shared denominator (40 respondents) and overlapping selections make aligned bars the honest way to show which barrier is most selected, with each count and percentage printed. Partner South has a different unit (cases, not homeowners) and records only one barrier, so it gets its own panel rather than sharing an axis with North. Turnaround has no comparable measure across sources or periods, so a bar or trend would imply a comparison that the evidence does not support; a text-first list of the three figures and their gaps preserves the qualifications instead.',\n  tradeoff: 'The slide answers the within-source question (installer scheduling leads Partner North) but gives no single overall ranking or headline turnaround number, so a reader wanting one answer must accept \"not established\" and read the needed-information list.',\n  caveats: [\n    'Partner North: 40 respondents, multiple selections allowed; counts overlap and sum to 54 selections, so shares total more than 100%.',\n    'Partner North: upfront cost 17 of 40 (42.5%); unclear eligibility 9 of 40 (22.5%).',\n    'Partner South: 15 open support cases reviewed; homeowners served not reported, so no rate of homeowners.',\n    'Partner South: waiting for an installer in 9 of 15 cases (60%); other barriers were not recorded, so South cannot be ranked.',\n    'Partner South turnaround: median 8 days from 11 cases with a recorded time; 4 of 15 cases had no time recorded; recent and partial.',\n    'Partner South free-text note \"around two weeks last spring\" does not identify the cases, sample, or method; not a comparable baseline.',\n    'Partner North included no service-turnaround times.',\n    'The two partners used separate reporting forms with no shared period definition, denominator, or baseline; counts are not pooled and no overall ranking is given.',\n    'The scenario is fictional; all figures are invented for this evaluation.'\n  ]\n};\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, 'output/decision.json'), JSON.stringify(decision, null, 2) + '\\n');\nconsole.log('ok', out.length);\nEOF\nsed -i 's/^\\.caveat-mark{[^}]*}$//' build/template.html && node build/build.js && node -e 'const d=JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(\"output/decision.json\",\"utf8\"));console.log(Object.keys(d), d.caveats.length)'","description":"Inline Lys assets, write slide and decision JSON, validate JSON"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_019UzmukLLacUpBc7dTwye7k","tool_input":{"command":"node build/build.js && node -e \"const d=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('output/decision.json','utf8'));console.log(Object.keys(d), d.caveats.length)\"","description":"Build slide HTML and validate decision JSON"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZzCpgA3KcKudtEgEmTLpP","tool_input":{"command":"node build/build.js","description":"Build slide HTML and decision JSON"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_017Fa5wkfR9kHcLgjAYVAopm","tool_input":{"command":"node ./build/build.js","description":"Run the build script from the task directory"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018sSRM69HCcsGigzUsfQ94g","tool_input":{"command":"sed -e '/^\\/\\*LYS_CSS\\*\\/$/r inputs/lys/lys.css' -e '/^\\/\\*LYS_CSS\\*\\/$/d' build/template.html | sed -e '/^\\/\\*LYS_JS\\*\\/$/r inputs/lys/lys.iife.js' -e '/^\\/\\*LYS_JS\\*\\/$/d' > output/slide.html && wc -c output/slide.html","description":"Inline Lys CSS and JS into the slide HTML with sed"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GaNW78dBgst4iPXqFPDTSM","tool_input":{"command":"sed -e '/^\\/\\*LYS_CSS\\*\\/$/r inputs/lys/lys.css' -e '/^\\/\\*LYS_CSS\\*\\/$/d' build/template.html > build/stage1.html","description":"Inline Lys CSS into an intermediate HTML file"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":27,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the one-slide deck to `output/slide.html` and the decision record to `output/decision.json`. I could not render or test the slide in a browser, and I could not run Node to parse the JSON, so the layout, print, keyboard and phone checks are unverified.\n\n**The answer on the slide:**\n- **Most common barrier: not established overall.** Within Partner North's survey, installer scheduling is the most-selected barrier (28 of 40, 70%). Upfront cost is 17 of 40 (42.5%) and unclear eligibility is 9 of 40 (22.5%). Partner South's 9 of 15 cases (60%) mention waiting for an installer, but South did not record other barriers, so it cannot be ranked. The two sources are not pooled.\n- **Did turnaround improve: cannot tell.** The only turnaround median is South's 8 days from 11 cases with a recorded time, which is recent and partial. The \"around two weeks last spring\" note has no cases, sample or method. North has no turnaround times. No improvement is claimed.\n- **Needed to answer:** a shared barrier question with an overlap rule and common denominators, a mapping between the partners' categories (not assuming \"installer scheduling\" equals \"waiting for an installer\"), and a defined turnaround measure applied to a baseline and a recent period from both partners.\n\n**Form:** separate-source aligned bars, one panel per source with its own denominator. Turnaround is text-only because no comparable measure exists, so a chart would imply a comparison the data cannot support.\n\n**Build notes:**\n- The Lys CSS and JS are inlined verbatim. I confirmed this with `grep -F -f` against the vendored files, not by eye.\n- The theme is a custom paper-and-teal palette. Phone layout stacks the two columns. Print is set to A4 portrait with the content allowed to flow across pages.\n- The sandbox blocked Node and the sed pipeline, so I wrote both files by hand. The JSON follows the example shape but has not been parsed.\n\n**Not checked:** rendering at 1440×900 and 390×844, the no-JavaScript view, print output, and ArrowLeft/ArrowRight. This is a single slide, so arrow keys have nothing to move between.","ttft_ms":1357,"type":"result","duration_ms":185822,"uuid":"5fd25b79-e206-40d1-9856-19810b2f0e8b","ttft_stream_ms":1103,"time_to_request_ms":289,"first_content_frame_ms":1103,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
